  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 1015 PM CDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nOctober is set to finish on a cool and wet note as an active \nsouthern jet stream returns complete with a contribution of richer \nmoisture from Tropical Storm Vance in the eastern Pacific. Until \nthen, Wednesday will be our mildest and driest day of the week after \na bout of morning stratus and some fog. Models remain in good \nagreement with a shortwave trough arriving in southwest flow \nThursday night into Friday morning accompanied by PWATs jumping from \n0.5\" to 1.5\". This surge of moisture and ample lift all point to \nanother regional precip event with heavy rain certainly in the \ncards. Recent deterministic and AI models are more keen to sweep \nthis moisture away beginning Saturday which is not yet reflected in \nthe NBM, but we suspect this theme will work its way into subsequent \nNBM runs. Thereafter, another window for precip may open as soon as \nSunday ahead of a vigorous upper low progged to curl S-SE from the \nnorthern Rockies accompanied by a cold front at some point early \nnext week.",
